{"url": "http://tmi.utexas.edu/academics/graduate-materials-science-engineering-program/prospective-students/", "final_url": "http://tmi.utexas.edu/academics/graduate-program", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-22", "text": "Graduate Program\nSkip to main content\nGive\nEntire Site Search\n\u2630\nHome\nAbout\nAcademics\nOverview\nUndergraduate Minor\nGraduate Program\nStudent Community\nProspective Students\nPeople\nResearch\nFacilities\nNews and Events\nPublications\nHome\nAbout\nOverview\nLeadership\nVisit Us\nContact Us\nAcademics\nOverview\nUndergraduate Minor\nGraduate Program\nStudent Community\nProspective Students\nPeople\nOverview\nFaculty Directory\nStaff Directory\nCore Faculty\nGraduate Studies Committee\nExecutive Committee\nUndergraduate Education Committee\nResearch\nOverview\nEnergy Materials\nNanomaterials\nStructural Materials\nElectronic and Photonic Materials\nPolymers and Biomaterials\nComputational Materials Science\nMaterials Characterization\nFacilities\nOverview\nMaterials Analysis and Spectroscopy Facility\nCleanroom Nanofabrication Facility\nElectron Microscopy Facility\nUser Information\nTrainings & Materials\nNews and Events\nOverview\nCalendar\nSeminars\nNewsletter\nOutreach\nPublications\nAcademics\nAcademics\nOverview\nUndergraduate Minor\nMinor Requirements\nHow to Apply\nOptional Courses\nFrequently Asked Questions\nGraduate Program\nDoctoral Program\nMaster's Program\nAdmissions\nFunding\nCourses\nThrust Areas\nFrequently Asked Questions\nStudent Community\nProspective Students\nFAQs\nGraduate Program\n100%\nOf Ph.D. Students Funded\nTop 14\nGraduate Program in the US\nU.S. News and World Report\nWhy apply to this program?\n1. We offer an interdisciplinary program.\nStudents are able to study core materials subjects while also developing depth within a specific area that cuts across multiple areas of science and engineering.\n2. Top ranked graduate education.\nThe Materials Science & Engineering Graduate Program is part of the Cockrell School of Engineering, which consistently receives high rankings in U.S. News and World Report.\n3. Excellent funding opportunities.\nFunding opportunities within the program typically provide a stipend, medical benefits, and tuition coverage. Almost all students in the program have a funding package of this quality.\n4. We produce professionally competitive applicants.\nOur students frequently find exceptional jobs in industry, at research labs, and in academia after graduation.\n5. World renowned faculty.\nCore faculty and members our Graduate Studies Committee and are responsible for supervising students, course advising, graduate student instruction, and curriculum review.\nContact Us\nAlyssa Peterson\nGraduate Program Coordinator II\nAdmissions: mseadmissions@austin.utexas.edu\nGeneral: mse@austin.utexas.edu\nYuebing Zheng, Ph.D.\nGraduate Advisor\nzheng@austin.utexas.edu\nAPPLY NOW\nAt A Glance\nProgram Starts:\nFall/Spring/Summer\nDeadline to Apply:\nSeptember 15th(Spring) December 1st(Fall)\nCredit Hours Required:\n65+\nSchedule:\nFull-time or part-time permitted per discussion with program head\nProgram Location:\nOn campus\nGRE Required:\nNo\nFALL 2027 RECRUITMENT PROJECTS\n\u00a9 The University of Texas at Austin | Privacy Policy | Web Accessibility\nCockrell School of Engineering\nCollege of Natural Sciences\nResources\nContact Us\nENGR Direct\nFaculty Directory\nInstrumentation Reservations\nSeminars\nStaff Directory\nGraduate Student Handbook\nUT Directory\nGive", "links": [["Skip to main content", "http://tmi.utexas.edu/academics/graduate-program#content"], ["", "http://tmi.utexas.edu/"], ["Give", "https://give.utexas.edu/?menu=OGPENDS&amount=500&response=DJ3TMI&solicit=TMI&srccsu=EN&comments=Texas%20Materials%20Institute%20%2830-2107-4493%2C%20407/13%29"], ["Home", "http://tmi.utexas.edu/"], ["About", "http://tmi.utexas.edu/about"], ["Academics", "http://tmi.utexas.edu/academics"], ["Overview", "http://tmi.utexas.edu/academic